{"id": "unknown-2026-11-25-006", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Counterpoint: an 8.6-Gen line cuts the cost of an 11.1\" iPad Pro OLED panel by 39% compared to a 6-Gen line", "content": "<p>Counterpoint Research released its latest IT Display Cost Report, which analyzes the manufacturing costs of OLED and LCD panels for tablets, laptops and monitors from 2024 to 2030. According to Counterpoint, an 11.1-inch iPad Pro OLED panel produced at an 8.6-Gen fab costs about 39% less to make in 2026 than the same panel produced at a 6-Gen fab.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/mcp-uploads/Counterpoint-8-6-Gen-iPad-Pro-OLED-cost-vs-6-Gen.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img cl", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/counterpoint-86-gen-line-cuts-cost-ipad-pro-oled-panel-39-compared-6-gen-line", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "boe-2026-11-25-007", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["boe"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "BOE reportedly in talks to acquire Visionox", "content": "<p>According to a report from Korea, BOE is in talks to acquire Chinese AMOLED producer <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/visionox\">Visionox</a>. BOE initially looked to buy one of Visionox's OLED production lines, but the talks have since expanded to a possible takeover of the entire company.</p><img class=\"align-center align-center\" src=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/styles/webp_format/public/mcp-uploads/Visionox-headquarters-photo.jpg.webp?itok=_W5Mgj3n\" alt=\"Visionox headqua", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/boe-reportedly-talks-acquire-visionox", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-11-25-008", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration", "mini_led"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung Display makes its biggest microLED move yet, to acquire a 9.1% stake in ams OSRAM for $230 million", "content": "<p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-oled\">Samsung Display</a> announced that it has signed an agreement to acquire a 9.1% stake in <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/osram-oled\">ams OSRAM</a> for around $230 million, which will make it the European LED and sensor maker's largest shareholder. The two companies have also formed a strategic partnership to jointly develop and commercialize a novel \"ultra-small\" microLED technology for displays. This is Samsung Display's most significant mi", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-display-makes-its-biggest-microled-move-yet-acquire-91-stake-ams-osram", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-25-009", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "OLED Emitter Systems, Part 3: TADF - the generation that became a supporting actor", "content": "<p>The OLED emitter is the material at the heart of every pixel, the organic molecule that actually turns electricity into light. Everything else in the stack exists to deliver charge to it. The emitter is a key part in determining the display's color, efficiency and lifetime.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/2026-10/OLED-emitter-systems-part-3-tadf-infographic.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img class=\"align-center align-center\" src=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/oled-emitter-systems-part-3-tadf-generation-became-supporting-actor", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-25-010", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Infrared cash cow funds Kinko Optical's push into CPO, AR, and LEO satellites", "content": "Kinko Optical is leveraging profits from its booming infrared lens business to bankroll next-generation bets in co-packaged optics (CPO), augmented reality (AR) glasses, and low-Earth orbit (LEO) satellites, according to General Manager Yi-Fang Chen. While infrared growth is expected to moderate from the near-doubling seen in 2025 and 2026 to a more sustainable annual rate of 20%&ndash;25% starting in 2027, the company plans to continue expanding both internal and supplier production capacity to", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261125PD219/kinko-optical-cpo-leo-business-ar-glasses.html", "type": "rss"}]}
